Each adapted file says so in its header and lists what was changed (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):

  loss.py         <- autojev/loss.py             per-question weights, mask_logits, Python 3.10 typing
  optim.py        <- autojev/optim.py            fused AdamW falls back when unavailable, Python 3.10 typing
  distributed.py  <- autojev/distributed.py      gloo on CPU, broadcast of trainable parameters only, no PEP 695
  events.py       <- autojev/events.py           DECIDE_EVENTS variable, Python 3.10 (timezone.utc)
  calibrate.py    <- autojev/evaluate.py         fit_temperature and the metrics, on logits, without httpx
  protocol.py     <- pplx_decider/protocol.py    text only, tokenizer called directly, lists instead of tensors
  model.py        <- autojev/model.py and pplx_decider/model.py    joint readout at the markers, LoRA, v1.2 layout
  train.py        <- autojev/train.py            learning-rate schedule, token-budget micro-batches, DDP loop

